import{_ as e,o as i,c as o,a2 as r}from"./chunks/framework.D3PjbZL0.js";const m=JSON.parse('{"title":"The Index of Legal Provisions","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/92-法律条文索引.md","filePath":"en/92-法律条文索引.md"}'),a={name:"en/92-法律条文索引.md"};function n(s,t,d,l,c,h){return i(),o("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[r('<h1 id="the-index-of-legal-provisions" tabindex="-1">The Index of Legal Provisions <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-index-of-legal-provisions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Index of Legal Provisions&quot;">​</a></h1><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Document No.</td><td>92</td></tr><tr><td>Module</td><td>Appendices and Reference Materials</td></tr><tr><td>Core Keywords</td><td>legal index, Symbiotic Constitution, labor law, consumer protection law, supporting laws</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="i-index-notes" tabindex="-1">I. Index Notes <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-index-notes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Index Notes&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This index covers the principal legal documents currently in force in the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization and their core provisions, arranged by legal hierarchy and department. The scope of the index includes the Symbiotic Constitution, the Symbiotic Labor Law, the Consumer Protection Law, and the five supporting laws on education, medical care, housing, environment, and antitrust. Each entry lists the name of the law, the provision number, and a summary of the core content of the provision. This index is a reference tool; for the complete text of the legal provisions and judicial interpretations, refer to the official texts of the respective laws.</p><h2 id="ii-the-symbiotic-constitution" tabindex="-1">II. The Symbiotic Constitution <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-the-symbiotic-constitution" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. The Symbiotic Constitution&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Symbiotic Constitution is the fundamental law of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, possessing the highest legal effect, enacted at the time of the formal establishment of the symbiotic civilization.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Provision No.</th><th>Core Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Article 1</td><td>Establishes the Hengyuan Universe (the Wanling Hengmao Origin Universe) as the governed domain of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization; the fundamental purpose of the symbiotic civilization is to achieve the symbiosis of the Ten Thousand Races and the ascension of the universe</td></tr><tr><td>Article 2</td><td>Establishes anti-predation as the fundamental stance of the civilization, prohibiting predatory cultivation and resource predation of any form</td></tr><tr><td>Article 3</td><td>Establishes &quot;returning the right to choose destiny and evolution to all living beings&quot; as the core concept of the civilization</td></tr><tr><td>Article 4</td><td>Establishes more work, more gain; autonomous growth; a path for everyone; and the common advancement of the Ten Thousand Races as the basic policies of the civilization</td></tr><tr><td>Article 5</td><td>Establishes the free opening system of the Three Hundred Origin Cultivation Systems; no organization or individual may monopolize the transmission rights of cultivation systems</td></tr><tr><td>Article 6</td><td>Establishes the Output-Linked Contract Mechanism as the basic resource distribution system</td></tr><tr><td>Article 7</td><td>Establishes the 20% Activation Strategy as a phased national goal</td></tr><tr><td>Article 8</td><td>Establishes the principle of Reality as the Foundation: the real world is the only real world, and fictional settings have no legal effect</td></tr><tr><td>Article 9</td><td>Establishes the Four-Stage Ascension Path as the long-term development strategy of the civilization</td></tr><tr><td>Article 10</td><td>Establishes the principle of equality of the Ten Thousand Races; all life forms are equal before the law</td></tr><tr><td>Article 11</td><td>Establishes the principle of symbiotic evolution; individual evolution must not come at the cost of the evolution rights of other individuals or collectives</td></tr><tr><td>Article 12</td><td>Establishes the principle of more work, more gain; resource distribution is based on contribution as the core basis</td></tr><tr><td>Article 13</td><td>Establishes the principle of autonomous growth; the autonomous evolution choice right of every life is respected</td></tr><tr><td>Article 14</td><td>Establishes the principle of a path for everyone; the state has the obligation to provide every life with a basic evolution path and resource guarantee</td></tr><tr><td>Article 15</td><td>Establishes the principle of sustainability; all development must take into account the sustainability of the origin of the universe</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 16–25</td><td>Provide for the basic rights of all living beings: the right to choose evolution, the right to obtain cultivation resources, the right to equal protection, the right to participate in symbiosis, the right to cultural preservation, the right to relief and appeal, the right to personal freedom, the right to personal dignity, the right to freedom of belief, and the right to freedom of expression</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 26–31</td><td>Provide for the basic obligations of all living beings: the obligation to abide by the law, to maintain the symbiotic order, to contribute through labor, to protect the environment, to respect the rights of others, and to guide junior cultivators</td></tr><tr><td>Article 32</td><td>Establishes the Anchor Assembly as the supreme organ of power, composed of representatives of the Ten Thousand Races in proportion</td></tr><tr><td>Article 33</td><td>Establishes the Symbiotic Executive Committee as the supreme administrative organ</td></tr><tr><td>Article 34</td><td>Establishes the Symbiotic Court as the supreme judicial organ, independently exercising judicial power</td></tr><tr><td>Article 35</td><td>Establishes the Anchor Oversight Committee as an independent oversight organ</td></tr><tr><td>Article 36</td><td>Provides for the legislative procedure: a legal bill is passed by a majority of more than half of the Anchor Assembly</td></tr><tr><td>Article 37</td><td>Provides for the constitutional amendment procedure: it must be passed by a majority of more than two-thirds of the Anchor Assembly and approved by more than half of the population through a referendum</td></tr><tr><td>Article 38</td><td>Establishes the constitutional review system; the Symbiotic Court has the power to declare laws that violate the Constitution null and void</td></tr><tr><td>Article 39</td><td>Establishes the constitutional litigation system; all living beings may directly initiate litigation in accordance with the Constitution</td></tr><tr><td>Article 40</td><td>Provides for the local autonomy system; each star domain and each plane implements autonomy within the framework of the Constitution</td></tr><tr><td>Article 41</td><td>Establishes the republic system of the Ten Thousand Races; all races are equal in the symbiotic civilization and implement regional autonomy</td></tr><tr><td>Article 42</td><td>Provides for the economic system of the symbiotic civilization: based on output-linked contracts, with multiple forms of ownership developing together</td></tr><tr><td>Article 43</td><td>Provides for the system of state ownership and fair distribution of cultivation resources</td></tr><tr><td>Article 44</td><td>Establishes the system of educational equity, guaranteeing the equal right to education of every life</td></tr><tr><td>Article 45</td><td>Establishes the universal medical security system</td></tr><tr><td>Article 46</td><td>Establishes the housing security system, guaranteeing the basic right to housing of every life</td></tr><tr><td>Article 47</td><td>Provides for the basic principles of cross-plane interaction; unauthorized cross-plane travel is prohibited</td></tr><tr><td>Article 48</td><td>Provides that the lawful outputs of archaeological activities are limited to abstract knowledge and information; the return of matter and energy is prohibited</td></tr><tr><td>Article 49</td><td>Provides for the basic principles of time regression; the principle of observing first and then intervening within limits must be followed</td></tr><tr><td>Article 50</td><td>Provides that the power to interpret the Constitution belongs to the Symbiotic Court, and the power to amend the Constitution belongs to the Anchor Assembly</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="iii-the-symbiotic-labor-law" tabindex="-1">III. The Symbiotic Labor Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-the-symbiotic-labor-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. The Symbiotic Labor Law&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Symbiotic Labor Law is the basic law regulating labor relations and protecting the rights and interests of workers, enacted on the legislative basis of Article 42 of the Symbiotic Constitution.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Provision No.</th><th>Core Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Article 1</td><td>Legislative purpose: to regulate labor relations, protect the lawful rights and interests of workers, and build harmonious and symbiotic labor relations</td></tr><tr><td>Article 2</td><td>Scope of application: all labor relations within the Hengyuan Universe, including material labor, cultivation labor, and creative labor</td></tr><tr><td>Article 3</td><td>Establishes the principle of equal employment of workers; employment discrimination based on race, gender, cultivation level, or origin is prohibited</td></tr><tr><td>Article 4</td><td>Establishes the principle of free choice of employment; forced labor and slavery are prohibited</td></tr><tr><td>Article 5</td><td>Provides for the labor contract system; a written labor contract shall be concluded when establishing a labor relationship</td></tr><tr><td>Article 6</td><td>Provides for the mandatory clauses of a labor contract: term of the contract, work content, labor remuneration, working hours, labor protection, and social insurance</td></tr><tr><td>Article 7</td><td>Establishes the eight-hour working day and the working hour system of no more than forty-four hours per week</td></tr><tr><td>Article 8</td><td>Provides for overtime restrictions: overtime shall not exceed one hour per day, or three hours under special circumstances, and shall not exceed thirty-six hours per month</td></tr><tr><td>Article 9</td><td>Provides for overtime wage standards: 1.5 times the wage for overtime on working days, 2 times the wage for overtime on rest days, and 3 times the wage for overtime on statutory holidays</td></tr><tr><td>Article 10</td><td>Establishes the minimum wage guarantee system; the minimum wage standard is formulated by each star domain according to local conditions</td></tr><tr><td>Article 11</td><td>Provides for the wage payment system: wages shall be paid monthly to the worker personally in monetary form, and shall not be withheld or delayed without cause</td></tr><tr><td>Article 12</td><td>Establishes the distribution principle of more work, more gain; a distribution system with distribution according to work as the main body and multiple distribution methods coexisting is implemented</td></tr><tr><td>Article 13</td><td>Provides for the labor safety and health system; employers must provide workers with labor safety and health conditions that meet the standards</td></tr><tr><td>Article 14</td><td>Provides for the protection of special groups: special labor protection is implemented for minor workers, female workers, disabled workers, and workers with low cultivation levels</td></tr><tr><td>Article 15</td><td>Establishes the vocational training system; employers have the obligation to provide vocational skills training for workers</td></tr><tr><td>Article 16</td><td>Provides for the labor rights and interests of cultivators: cultivation labor is equally protected by this Law, and the ownership of cultivation results is agreed upon by contract</td></tr><tr><td>Article 17</td><td>Establishes the social insurance system for workers: pension insurance, medical insurance, unemployment insurance, work-related injury insurance, and maternity insurance</td></tr><tr><td>Article 18</td><td>Provides for the welfare system for workers: employers shall provide workers with necessary welfare benefits</td></tr><tr><td>Article 19</td><td>Establishes the labor dispute handling system: a four-level handling mechanism of consultation, mediation, arbitration, and litigation</td></tr><tr><td>Article 20</td><td>Provides for the trade union system; workers have the right to organize and join trade unions in accordance with the law to protect their lawful rights and interests</td></tr><tr><td>Article 21</td><td>Provides for the collective contract system; trade unions represent workers in concluding collective contracts with employers</td></tr><tr><td>Article 22</td><td>Provides that the rules and regulations of an employer shall be discussed by the workers&#39; congress or all workers</td></tr><tr><td>Article 23</td><td>Provides for the conditions and procedures for the termination of labor contracts</td></tr><tr><td>Article 24</td><td>Provides for the economic compensation system; employers shall pay economic compensation when lawfully terminating labor contracts</td></tr><tr><td>Article 25</td><td>Provides for the compensation system for unlawful termination of labor contracts</td></tr><tr><td>Article 26</td><td>Establishes the labor dispatch management system, regulating labor dispatch employment</td></tr><tr><td>Article 27</td><td>Provides for the special rules for part-time employment</td></tr><tr><td>Article 28</td><td>Provides for the supervision and inspection system; labor administrative departments supervise and inspect the compliance of employers with labor laws and regulations in accordance with the law</td></tr><tr><td>Article 29</td><td>Provides for legal liability: employers who violate this Law shall bear administrative, civil, and criminal liability in accordance with the law</td></tr><tr><td>Article 30</td><td>Provides for the effective date and the power of interpretation of this Law</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="iv-the-consumer-protection-law" tabindex="-1">IV. The Consumer Protection Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-the-consumer-protection-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. The Consumer Protection Law&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The Consumer Protection Law is the basic law protecting the lawful rights and interests of consumers and regulating the conduct of business operators.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Provision No.</th><th>Core Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Article 1</td><td>Legislative purpose: to protect the lawful rights and interests of consumers, maintain the social economic order, and promote the healthy development of the symbiotic market economy</td></tr><tr><td>Article 2</td><td>Scope of application: the protection of the rights and interests of consumers within the Hengyuan Universe when purchasing, using commodities or receiving services for the needs of daily life</td></tr><tr><td>Article 3</td><td>Establishes the basic principles of transactions between business operators and consumers: voluntariness, equality, fairness, and good faith</td></tr><tr><td>Article 4</td><td>Establishes the principle that the state protects the lawful rights and interests of consumers; the state takes measures to guarantee that consumers exercise their rights in accordance with the law</td></tr><tr><td>Article 5</td><td>Provides for the nine basic rights of consumers: the right to safety, the right to information, the right to free choice, the right to fair dealing, the right to claim compensation, the right to association, the right to knowledge, the right to respect, and the right to supervision</td></tr><tr><td>Article 6</td><td>Provides for the consumer&#39;s right to safety: consumers enjoy the right that their personal and property safety is not harmed when purchasing and using commodities and receiving services</td></tr><tr><td>Article 7</td><td>Provides for the consumer&#39;s right to information: consumers enjoy the right to know the true information of the commodities they purchase or use and the services they receive</td></tr><tr><td>Article 8</td><td>Provides for the consumer&#39;s right to free choice: consumers enjoy the right to freely choose commodities or services</td></tr><tr><td>Article 9</td><td>Provides for the consumer&#39;s right to fair dealing: consumers enjoy the right to fair dealing and have the right to refuse coercive transactions</td></tr><tr><td>Article 10</td><td>Provides for the consumer&#39;s right to claim compensation: consumers who suffer personal or property damage due to the purchase and use of commodities or the receipt of services enjoy the right to obtain compensation in accordance with the law</td></tr><tr><td>Article 11</td><td>Provides for the basic obligations of business operators: to perform statutory and agreed obligations, accept supervision, ensure safety, provide true information, issue vouchers, guarantee quality, perform the three guarantees, refrain from unfair dealing, and refrain from infringing personal dignity</td></tr><tr><td>Article 12</td><td>Provides for the safety guarantee obligation of business operators: business operators shall guarantee that the commodities or services they provide meet the requirements of protecting personal and property safety</td></tr><tr><td>Article 13</td><td>Provides for the information disclosure obligation of business operators: business operators shall provide consumers with true information about the commodities or services, and shall not make false or misleading publicity</td></tr><tr><td>Article 14</td><td>Provides for the special norms for cultivation products and services: business operators of cultivation methods, cultivation instruments, and energy products must possess special qualifications, and the products must pass safety certification</td></tr><tr><td>Article 15</td><td>Provides for the regulation of standard terms: business operators shall not use standard terms to exclude or limit consumer rights, or to mitigate or exempt the operator&#39;s liability</td></tr><tr><td>Article 16</td><td>Provides for the seven-day no-reason return system: consumers who purchase commodities through remote methods such as the network have the right to return the commodities within seven days from the date of receipt</td></tr><tr><td>Article 17</td><td>Provides for the three guarantees system: if the commodities or services provided by business operators do not meet quality requirements, consumers may request repair, replacement, or return in accordance with national regulations</td></tr><tr><td>Article 18</td><td>Provides for the punitive damages system: if business operators engage in fraudulent conduct in providing commodities or services, they shall, in accordance with the requirements of consumers, increase compensation for the losses suffered, with the increased compensation amount being three times the price of the commodities purchased or the cost of the services received by the consumer</td></tr><tr><td>Article 19</td><td>Provides for consumer organizations: consumers&#39; associations and other consumer organizations are social organizations lawfully established to carry out social supervision over commodities and services and to protect the lawful rights and interests of consumers</td></tr><tr><td>Article 20</td><td>Provides for the channels for resolving consumer disputes: negotiation and settlement with business operators, requesting mediation by consumers&#39; associations, appealing to relevant administrative departments, submitting to arbitration, and initiating litigation in court</td></tr><tr><td>Article 21</td><td>Provides for the reversal of the burden of proof in disputes: for durable commodities or services such as decoration, if consumers discover defects within six months from the date of receipt, the business operator bears the burden of proof</td></tr><tr><td>Article 22</td><td>Provides for the administrative and criminal liability of business operators</td></tr><tr><td>Article 23</td><td>Provides for the effective date and the power of interpretation of this Law</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-the-five-supporting-laws" tabindex="-1">V. The Five Supporting Laws <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-the-five-supporting-laws" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. The Five Supporting Laws&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="_5-1-the-education-guarantee-law" tabindex="-1">5.1 The Education Guarantee Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-1-the-education-guarantee-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.1 The Education Guarantee Law&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Provision No.</th><th>Core Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Article 1</td><td>Legislative purpose: to guarantee the equal right to education of all living beings, build a symbiotic education system, and promote the common development of the cultures of the Ten Thousand Races</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 2–5</td><td>Establish the principle of educational equity, the principle of free education (at the basic education stage), the principle of educational diversity, and the principle of educational innovation</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 6–10</td><td>Provide for the system architecture of preschool education, compulsory education, upper secondary education, higher education, and cultivation education</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 11–15</td><td>Provide for the special systems of cultivation education: the teaching norms of the Three Hundred Systems, the mentor system, and the cultivation resource allocation system</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 16–20</td><td>Provide for the rights and obligations of teachers, the teacher qualification system, and the guarantee of teacher treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 21–25</td><td>Provide for education investment guarantee, education facility construction, educational informatization, special education, and cross-race education</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 26–30</td><td>Provide for the education evaluation system, the education supervision system, legal liability, and supplementary provisions</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="_5-2-the-medical-security-law" tabindex="-1">5.2 The Medical Security Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-2-the-medical-security-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.2 The Medical Security Law&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Provision No.</th><th>Core Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Article 1</td><td>Legislative purpose: to establish a universal medical security system, guarantee the right to health of all living beings, and improve the overall health level of the Ten Thousand Races</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 2–5</td><td>Establish the principle of universal medical insurance, the principle of free basic medical care, the principle of integrating Chinese and Western medicine, and the principle of incorporating cultivation medicine</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 6–10</td><td>Provide for the multi-level medical insurance system of basic medical insurance, critical illness insurance, medical assistance, and commercial health insurance</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 11–15</td><td>Provide for medical institution management, the medical personnel system, medical quality and safety, and the special norms of cultivation medicine</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 16–20</td><td>Provide for drug management, medical device management, energy medical product management, and the essential drugs system</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 21–25</td><td>Provide for the public health system, disease prevention and control, health education, cross-race medical care, and medical security for special groups</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 26–30</td><td>Provide for medical dispute handling, medical supervision, legal liability, and supplementary provisions</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="_5-3-the-housing-security-law" tabindex="-1">5.3 The Housing Security Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-3-the-housing-security-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.3 The Housing Security Law&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Provision No.</th><th>Core Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Article 1</td><td>Legislative purpose: to guarantee the basic right to housing of all living beings, build a multi-level housing security system, and achieve housing for all</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 2–5</td><td>Establish the principle of housing right guarantee, the principle of housing equity, the principle of both renting and purchasing, and the principle of sustainable housing</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 6–10</td><td>Provide for the housing supply system of public rental housing, subsidized rental housing, shared-ownership housing, and commercial housing</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 11–15</td><td>Provide for the housing provident fund system, the housing subsidy system, first-home support policies, and special housing policies for cultivators</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 16–20</td><td>Provide for housing construction standards, the application of spatial technology in housing, green buildings, and age-friendly and barrier-free housing</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 21–25</td><td>Provide for real estate market regulation, rental housing market norms, property service management, and housing maintenance guarantee</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 26–30</td><td>Provide for housing security supervision, legal liability, and supplementary provisions</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="_5-4-the-environmental-protection-law" tabindex="-1">5.4 The Environmental Protection Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-4-the-environmental-protection-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.4 The Environmental Protection Law&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Provision No.</th><th>Core Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Article 1</td><td>Legislative purpose: to protect and improve the environment, prevent and control pollution and other public hazards, guarantee public health, promote the construction of cosmic ecological civilization, and advance sustainable development</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 2–5</td><td>Establish the principle of protection priority, the principle of prevention first, the principle of comprehensive treatment, the principle of public participation, and the principle of liability for damage</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 6–10</td><td>Provide for the environmental supervision and management system, the environmental standard system, the environmental impact assessment system, the environmental monitoring system, and cross-plane environmental management</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 11–15</td><td>Provide for air pollution prevention and control, water pollution prevention and control, soil pollution prevention and control, energy pollution prevention and control, and law pollution prevention and control</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 16–20</td><td>Provide for solid waste treatment, noise pollution prevention and control, radioactive pollution prevention and control, ecological protection, and biodiversity protection</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 21–25</td><td>Provide for the environmental impact control of cultivation activities, the ecological protection of energy extraction, and the environmental requirements of cross-plane archaeology</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 26–30</td><td>Provide for information disclosure and public participation, environmental public interest litigation, legal liability, and supplementary provisions</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="_5-5-the-antimonopoly-law" tabindex="-1">5.5 The Antimonopoly Law <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-5-the-antimonopoly-law" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;5.5 The Antimonopoly Law&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Provision No.</th><th>Core Content</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Article 1</td><td>Legislative purpose: to prevent and stop monopolistic conduct, protect fair market competition, improve the efficiency of economic operation, safeguard the interests of consumers and the public interest of society, and promote the healthy development of the symbiotic market economy</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 2–5</td><td>Establish the foundational position of competition policy, the fair competition review system, the prohibition of monopoly agreements, the prohibition of abuse of market dominance, and the control of concentration of undertakings</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 6–10</td><td>Provide for the identification and exemption of monopoly agreements, horizontal monopoly agreements, vertical monopoly agreements, and monopolistic conduct of industry associations</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 11–15</td><td>Provide for the identification of market dominance, the types of conduct constituting abuse of market dominance, and the prohibition of predatory pricing</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 16–20</td><td>Provide for the filing standards for concentration of undertakings, the review procedure, additional restrictive conditions, and decisions prohibiting concentration</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 21–25</td><td>Provide for the special prohibition of monopoly in cultivation systems: prohibiting the monopoly of cultivation methods, prohibiting the monopoly of cultivation resources, and prohibiting the monopoly of mentor networks</td></tr><tr><td>Articles 26–30</td><td>Provide for the antitrust enforcement authority, the investigation procedure, legal liability, the leniency system, and supplementary provisions</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The index of legal provisions is the reference map of the rule-of-law system of the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization. From the Symbiotic Constitution as the fundamental law, to the Labor Law and the Consumer Protection Law regulating people&#39;s livelihood, and then to the five supporting laws, together they constitute a complete legal system &quot;with the Constitution as the commander, the basic laws as the backbone, and the supporting laws as the support&quot;. This system ensures that all activities of the symbiotic civilization operate on the track of the rule of law, providing a solid institutional guarantee for the common advancement of the Ten Thousand Races.</p><h2 id="related-documents" tabindex="-1">Related Documents <a class="header-anchor" href="#related-documents" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related Documents&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>40-共生宪法总纲 (Symbiotic Constitution: General Principles)</li><li>41-共生劳动法 (Symbiotic Labor Law)</li><li>48-司法体系与裁决机制 (Judicial System and Adjudication Mechanism)</li></ul>',28)])])}const p=e(a,[["render",n]]);export{m as __pageData,p as default};
